{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2180-04-12 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I’m Dr. Lee, one of the surgery team doctors. You’re here today for a planned procedure on your right arm fistula because of steal syndrome, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2180-04-12 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. My hand’s been cold and painful for weeks. It gets worse after dialysis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2180-04-12 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. Steal syndrome means too much blood is going into the fistula and not enough to your hand. We’re going to do a banding procedure to reduce the flow and help your hand get more blood."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2180-04-12 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had this done before. It helped for a while. Is this the same thing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2180-04-12 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s the same procedure—banding the fistula. It’s less invasive than removing it completely. We hope it will relieve your symptoms again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2180-04-12 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I can still use the fistula for dialysis after?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2180-04-12 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s the goal—to keep it working for dialysis while fixing the hand pain. We’ll check it after the procedure and again tomorrow during dialysis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2180-04-12 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. I’m a little nervous, but I trust you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2180-04-12 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll take good care of you. You’ll go to the operating room around noon. After that, you’ll wake up in the recovery area, then come back here to your room."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2180-04-12 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, you’re back. How are you feeling after the procedure?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2180-04-12 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A bit groggy, but okay. My arm feels tight, but not painful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2180-04-12 12:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s normal. We’ve banded the fistula, and the dressing is snug. You’ll get pain medicine if you need it. We’ll also check your hand’s color and warmth often."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2180-04-12 12:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I eat? I’m kind of hungry."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2180-04-12 12:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you can have a regular diet. We’ll start you on your home medications too, including your blood thinner, warfarin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2180-04-12 12:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I take a lot of meds, but I brought my list."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2180-04-12 12:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve reviewed it. Everything’s been restarted except your dialysis schedule, which will be tomorrow as planned."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2180-04-12 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just checking in. How’s your hand feeling now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2180-04-12 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s warmer than it’s been in weeks! The pain is much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2180-04-12 15:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s excellent. It means the banding is working. We’ll keep monitoring it. Any chest pain or shortness of breath?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2180-04-12 15:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, not today. I had some last week, but it went away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2180-04-12 15:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did a chest X-ray just to be safe. It showed clear lungs and no issues. Your heart size is normal too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2180-04-12 15:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good to know. I was worried it might be my heart again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2180-04-12 15:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Given your history, we always check. But this time, it’s not cardiac. Your labs also look stable—your kidney function is as expected for dialysis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2180-04-12 18:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Doctor, can I take my pain meds? My arm is starting to ache."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2180-04-12 18:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you can take the Dilaudid as needed. Two milligrams every four hours. Let us know if it’s not helping."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2180-04-12 18:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I also take tramadol sometimes. Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2180-04-12 18:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll stick with Dilaudid for now since it’s stronger and works faster. We can switch back to tramadol when you’re home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2180-04-13 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You slept well? We’re going to do some blood work before dialysis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2180-04-13 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I did. Is the dialysis still scheduled for today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2180-04-13 07:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, at noon. We want to make sure the fistula works well after the banding. So far, the thrill is strong and your hand is warm."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2180-04-13 07:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I was worried it might not work after the surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2180-04-13 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We monitored it closely. The banding reduced flow just enough to help your hand without killing the fistula."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2180-04-13 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did great during dialysis. The team said the fistula functioned well, and your blood pressure stayed stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2180-04-13 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t feel dizzy or weak like I sometimes do. That’s a good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2180-04-13 13:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. And your hand is still warm and pink. We think you’re ready to go home today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2180-04-13 13:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great! What should I watch for at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2180-04-13 13:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call the access clinic if your hand becomes cold, blue, or painful, or if you can’t feel the thrill. Also for fever, swelling, or if the dressing gets wet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2180-04-13 13:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my meds? Should I change anything?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2180-04-13 13:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, go back to all your usual medications. We adjusted your warfarin dose slightly—now 3 mg daily. Your outpatient team will check your INR."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2180-04-13 13:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. No heavy lifting, no blood pressure checks on my arms, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2180-04-13 13:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Protect both arms. Wear loose sleeves and no tight jewelry. Follow up with your surgeon in a week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2180-04-13 13:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you so much. I feel much better already."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2180-04-13 13:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’re glad the procedure helped. You’ll be discharged in a few hours once the paperwork is ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2180-04-13 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a final check before you leave. How’s the pain now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2180-04-13 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Only mild discomfort. I took acetaminophen earlier and it helped."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2180-04-13 15:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Keep using acetaminophen for mild pain. Save the Dilaudid for if it gets worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2180-04-13 15:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I’ll keep doing dialysis as usual?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2180-04-13 15:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, exactly on schedule. The fistula is working well, so no changes there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2180-04-13 15:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m so glad this is behind me. Thank you again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2180-04-13 15:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing great. Take care, and call if anything changes."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2180-04-12 07:15:00",
    "admission_end": "2180-04-13 19:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A female patient with end-stage renal disease and a history of arteriovenous fistula complications was admitted for symptomatic steal syndrome in her right arm. She underwent a planned revision procedure—banding of the right arm arteriovenous fistula—to reduce blood flow and improve hand perfusion. The procedure was successful, with immediate improvement in hand pain and warmth. She tolerated postoperative recovery well, resumed hemodialysis without complications, and maintained stable vital signs and lab values. She was discharged home the following day with instructions to monitor for access site complications, continue her regular dialysis and medication regimen, and follow up with her surgical clinic. Her warfarin dose was adjusted to 3 mg daily during the admission.",
    "problems": [
      "Other complications due to renal dialysis device, implant, and graft",
      "Unspecified procedure as the cause of abnormal reaction of patient, or of later complication, without mention of misadventure at time of procedure",
      "Hypertensive chronic kidney disease, unspecified, with chronic kidney disease stage V or end stage renal disease",
      "End stage renal disease",
      "Kidney replaced by transplant",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Obstructive sleep apnea (adult)(pediatric)",
      "Other specified disorders of circulatory system",
      "Acquired absence of both cervix and uterus"
    ]
  }
}
